messages:
lina-sales: Heads up — AcmeHealth wants a short POC next week. Need a quick alignment on 3 asks: 1) a streaming SDK example (Go) that demonstrates function/tool calling + structured JSON output, 2) pricing for sustained ~500 qps (and how reserved capacity vs hosted compares), 3) SSO/KMS and SOC2 Qs their security team will send. Anyone able to jump on a short sync? cc @sam-pre-sales @matt-eng

sam-pre-sales: I can do tomorrow 10am PT. For pricing: at sustained 500 qps recommendation is Dedicated (reserved). Ballpark: reserved gives ~30–45% per-token cost savings vs hosted for heavy sustained usage, but need to validate commit level. Do they have burst characteristics?

lina-sales: They said baseline steady ~500 qps, occasional spikes 3x for 10–15m. I'll ask them for a ingestion trace before the call.

matt-eng: Quick notes on SDK/streaming: Use streaming client with an event handler that distinguishes partial tokens, tool_call events, and final structured output. For Go the pattern is like: 
```
// pseudo example
stream, _ := client.StreamCreate(ctx, req)
for evt := range stream.Events() {
  switch evt.Type {
  case "tool_call":
    // route to external adapter, capture tool_id + inputs
  case "partial":
    fmt.Print(evt.Text)
  case "structured":
    // evt.Payload contains JSON according to json_schema
  }
}
```
Include `json_schema` in the request so the model emits strict structured JSON (helps the adaptor). For function/tool calls make sure the adaptor returns a canonical `tool_result` object and we feed it back to the stream. I'll paste a full runnable gist before the meeting.

cait-security: For the SOC2/kms questions: we have a SOC2 report we can share via NDA. KMS options supported in Private/Dedicated: AWS KMS, GCP KMS; HSM via our Private deploy (customer-managed). If they require customer-controlled key material on-host, that pushes to Redwood Private. Also note: audit logs retention defaults to 90 days on hosted — can be extended on Dedicated. I can join first 10min to cover this.

akshay-pre: Pre-call checklist I suggest we follow: 1) confirm model family + quantization (FP16 vs int8) 2) sample payloads & expected tokens per request 3) traffic pattern (burst factor & cadence) 4) acceptable P95/P99 tail latency and SLA expectations 5) SSO flow details (SAML/OIDC) 6) security docs they need (SOC2, encryption at rest/in transit). I'll draft a 20min agenda.

ops-bot: Quote RC-2468 created for reserved capacity delta estimate — placeholder monthly commit attached. Link: https://console.redwood/quotes/RC-2468 (bot)

lina-sales: Awesome, locking 10am PT. @matt-eng pls drop the Go gist pre-meeting, @cait-security please join first 10 mins for KMS/SOC2 orientation. I'll push them to share an ingestion trace + sample payloads beforehand. :thumbsup:
